Author: James Peter <github@zemaj.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 19 15:03:23 2026 +1000

    Fix the tag-tier installer journey and the restart snapshot race
    
    The installer shard (tags, nightly, dispatch) failed in definitionsJourney:
    f47bdac relabelled the definition-file input for Pingdom, and the journey
    still waited on the old full label. Find the input by its stable
    "Definition file" prefix instead of pinning the copy.
    
    signed-runner's restart check read history (a console request that starts
    hosted work in waitUntil) after its snapshot, so a kick claimed 5 s after
    the last one wrote 'running' and was cut off by dispose. Read history
    first, then settle console work before the snapshot.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

